# Standing still on flat ground: nothing moves.
scenario stand_still
map bloodgulch
# <name> <x> <y> <z> <yaw, radians>: a little above the ground, so that the
# player settles on it in the first ticks
start flat_field 77.9 -166.2 0.32 0.0
ticks 120

# what the Rust simulation may differ from the C engine by: what walking on
# the ground reaches (its port of the engine's movement differs only by the
# rounding of its own square root, sine and cosine: at most 6e-5 world units
# and 4e-4 world units a second in the runs of these scenarios), with room
# for another machine's; a run of the C engine against itself allows none
tolerance position 0.001
tolerance velocity 0.005
tolerance facing 0.001
tolerance state 0
